  "source_shape_findings": [
    "Whole continuous three-storey cross-shaped main building retained, including occupied third-floor central room group, four full-height projecting upper wings, real recessed second-floor balconies and partial eastern B1 volume. No invented central courtyard or full-width basement.",
    "B1CW90/1FCCW90/2F180/3F original orientation verified using columns, diagonal stairs plus asymmetric paired/single crossed boxes and toilet strip. Earlier same-direction664 and +46cross-floor claim were withdrawn. Crossed boxes are geometric anchors, not elevator identification; inventory lists zero elevators.",
    "Common frame665 preserves projecting upper outline and smaller1F/main-column footprint. 662translation(+155,+200),664(x+100,y*.953+168),661*.777+(470,172) are diagram registration, not measured dimensions or independently proven structural offsets.",
    "First-model corrections are complete: actual east and west finite entrance recesses with rear door surfaces replace cut=None cosmetic windows. Northwestern and southeastern bent external stair interfaces are retained. A single photo-derived blank canopy/ramp candidate is on the west, not duplicated on opposite faces.",
    "North/west deeper roof-edge bands and finite short underside ribs are separate from lower third-floor projecting-floor soffits. East/south do not mirror the same deep eave. Pale upper shoulders are full-height sloped coarse proxies rather than just a bottom bevel; fine tile/curve dimensions remain approximate.",
    "Same archived v1mesh was independently tested at global180 west alternatives; final v2same-mesh658/659 westNW/SW views more directly fit deep-eave/shoulder evidence. EastSE/NE alternatives are not uniquely excluded. No compass, exact camera recovery, unique room-to-photo correspondence or per-photo mesh mirroring claimed.",
    "Western narrow perimeter footings meet the base while preserving underside air, unlike eastern partialB1. Balconies, entrance openings, two bent stairs and finite side ramp remain open/connected rather than filled for a single-shell result.",
    "No separateRF drawing was supplied. Complete upper main roof is a bounded flat closure; the small photographed rooftop object is omitted because exact position/use are not established. This documented simplification is not proof that the real roof has no object. Unknown sides use restrained regular-window proxies, not four-side photographic reconstruction.",
    "Seven opaque material groups carry no photo textures, lettering or source-plan pixels. Canonical STL/3MF/native vertices, face order, winding and per-face materials agree. Relative heights, colors, framing, local grade, ramp/stair details and shoulder curvature remain approximate."
  ],
